<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deir el-Bersha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deir el-Bersha is an ancient cemetery on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a>, opposite Mallawi. Its rock-cut tombs belonged mainly to the nomarchs of the Hare <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nome">nome</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a>. The tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djehutyhotep">Djehutyhotep</a> contains a famous scene of a colossal statue being dragged on a sledge by teams of workers.</p></div>
